The Paper in One Sentence

DeepSeek improves Transformers by making them vastly more efficient at scale, mainly through Mixture-of-Experts and a radically better attention mechanism that slashes KV-cache memory while preserving performance.

That’s the soul of the paper.

Why This Paper Exists (The Real Problem)

Transformers work brilliantly.
But at large scale, they hit two hard walls:

Computation cost explodes

Memory (KV cache) becomes the bottleneck

Especially during inference.

This paper is answering one question:

How can we scale Transformers to GPT-4-level sizes without drowning in compute and memory costs?

DeepSeek’s answer:
Don’t compute everything, and don’t store everything.

What This Paper Is NOT

❌ Not proposing a new Transformer from scratch

❌ Not changing attention theory

❌ Not introducing a new loss or training paradigm

Instead, it’s about engineering-level architectural improvements that make large models actually usable.

Mental Map of the Paper

The paper has three big ideas, stacked on top of the standard Transformer:

Mixture of Experts (MoE) → compute efficiency

Multi-Head Latent Attention (MLA) → memory efficiency

Decoupled RoPE → long-context accuracy without breaking compression

If you understand these three, you understand the paper.

